Maybe add a comment that this reuses the tuple impls?

Personally, I'd change it to use a custom struct, because I'd rather be able to do
```rust
struct MyThing<'a>{ local: Local<'a, u32> };
fn my_sys(f: MyThing){}
my_sys.system().configure(|value| value.0.local=Some(u32));
```
instead of the current
```rust
my_sys.system().configure(|value| value.0.0 =Some(u32));
```

@cart is there a reason that this doesn't create a custom struct which is a copy of T?

As a bonus this would get correct privacy for free, as well as allowing infinitely large `derive(SystemParam)` structs.
